📚 Akshara-Pi: The Zen of E-InkAkshara-Pi is a high-fidelity, distraction-free e-reading framework for the Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W. It prioritizes typography (Literata/Bookerly) and architectural efficiency to turn raw hardware into a "digital paper" experience.🏛️ System ArchitectureAkshara-Pi uses a Decoupled Pipeline:Ingestion (Python/MuPDF): Pre-renders EPUB/PDF into 1-bit bitmaps.Logic (C State Machine): Manages the UI, Library, and Page navigation.Hardware (SPI/LUT): Streams raw pixels to the E-ink controller at 10MHz.🛒 1. Bill of Materials (BOM)ComponentSpecificationPurposeSBCRaspberry Pi Zero 2 WCore processing and rendering engine.DisplayWaveshare 5.83" E-Paper (B/W)$648 \times 480$ resolution "pocket-book" canvas.AdapterWaveshare E-Paper HATPhysical SPI interface for the Pi Zero.Storage32GB MicroSD (Class 10)Storage for OS and 2,700+ pre-rendered books.Input5-Way Navigation SwitchTactical UI control (Up, Down, L, R, Enter).Power1200mAh LiPo + TP4056Portable power with USB-C charging.🛠️ 2. Hardware Setup & WiringIf using the Waveshare HAT, simply plug it onto the GPIO header. If wiring manually:VCC: 3.3V (Pin 1) | GND: Ground (Pin 6)DIN (MOSI): GPIO 10 (Pin 19) | CLK (SCK): GPIO 11 (Pin 23)CS: GPIO 8 (Pin 24) | D/C: GPIO 25 (Pin 22)RST: GPIO 17 (Pin 11) | BUSY: GPIO 24 (Pin 18)⚙️ 3. Software Configuration & InstallationStep A: System PreparationFlash Raspberry Pi OS Lite (64-bit).Enable SPI: sudo raspi-config -> Interface Options -> SPI -> Yes.Step B: DependenciesInstall the MuPDF rendering engine and the lgpio hardware library:Bashsudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y libmupdf-dev liblgpio-dev build-essential git
Step C: Build the EngineBashgit clone https://github.com/raviv99/Akshara-Pi.git
cd Akshara-Pi
make clean && make
🚀 4. Usage WorkflowAdd Content: Place .epub or .pdf files into the /books folder.Pre-Render: Run the ingestion script to create the bitmap cache:python3 scripts/ingest.py --input books/my_book.epub --output cache/my_book/Read: Launch the Akshara-Pi environment:sudo ./akshara_main🔍 5. Troubleshooting & MaintenanceGhosting: The system triggers a "Global Refresh" (Full Flash) every 10 pages to clean the ink.Busy Timeout: Ensure RST and BUSY pins are connected securely; check for 3.3V stability.Typography: Ensure Literata.ttf is in the /fonts directory before running the ingestion script.
